; Restores wpn_rpk74's icon, which renders as a garbled fragment in the
; inventory and the F7 debug spawner.
;
; MartinLore's Stalker 2 icons repoints the RPK family at the HD atlas
; ui\ui_stalker2_rifles by patching the parent section:
;
;   ![wpn_rpk]  icons_texture=ui\ui_stalker2_rifles  10x4 @ (52,12)  scale=2
;
; wpn_rpk74 inherits from wpn_rpk ([wpn_rpk74]:wpn_rpk in
; items/weapons/w_rpk.ltx, won by "410- 3DSS for GAMMA"), so it picks up the
; HD icons_texture and inv_grid_scale from the patched parent. But it also
; redeclares its own inv_grid_x/y/width/height, which are still the legacy
; ui_icon_equipment coordinates (5x2 @ 35,14). MartinLore patches
; wpn_rpk74_16 and wpn_rpk74_16_drum explicitly, but never plain wpn_rpk74,
; so nothing corrects them.
;
; The engine therefore samples a 250x100 window at (1750,700) out of the
; 4096x2048 HD atlas, a region belonging to unrelated weapons, and draws it
; in a ceil(5/2) x ceil(2/2) = 3x1 cell. That is the two disconnected pieces
; labelled "RPK-74" in the top-right of the debug spawner's By Icon panel.
;
; Fix: give wpn_rpk74 the parent's HD coordinates, i.e. restore the
; inheritance the override was silently breaking. Using wpn_rpk's 10x4 also
; keeps the item's inventory footprint at 5x2 cells (10/scale x 4/scale),
; matching what it occupied before the HD icon pack. Adopting
; wpn_rpk74_16's icon instead (12x4 @ 0,20) would be a closer visual match
; for the 5.45mm variant but would widen the footprint to 6x2 cells.
;
; Filename sorts after mod_system_zzzzzzzzzzzzzzz_s2rifles.ltx so this
; override is applied last.

![wpn_rpk74]
icons_texture      = ui\ui_stalker2_rifles
inv_grid_width     = 10
inv_grid_height    = 4
inv_grid_x         = 52
inv_grid_y         = 12
inv_grid_scale     = 2
